From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:01:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 088/138] ASoC: codecs: Add a reverse-engineered Cirrus Logic
 CS42L67 driver

The CS42L67 is the headset/microphone/receiver codec of the iPhone 6,
on SPI. There is no datasheet; the register access, ID check, power-up
and power-down sequences and the capture routing are taken from iOS'
AppleCS42L67Audio kext.

Supported: the XSP port as a TDM consumer, the four ADC channels with
their input muxes, MICBIAS1/3/4, four XSP TX source muxes, an
experimental mono headphone path (output group A, which may be wrong)
and an optional polled jack status (jack_poll, unverified register).

If the chip ID does not match the driver still registers its DAI and
widgets but never touches the chip (allow_missing, default on), so the
rest of the sound card binds.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
